p.src:
The last question asks whether money buys happiness. Perrin gives a restrained answer. Money may buy freedom if it is handled properly, but it does not automatically buy happiness. The operative variable is not merely amount. It is management capacity: $\begin{aligned}
\neg \text{Manage}(\$1{,}000)
&\Longrightarrow
\neg \text{Manage}(\$1{,}000{,}000),\\
\text{Money} + \text{Judgment}
&\to
\text{Freedom},\\
\text{Money}
&\neq
\text{Happiness}.\end{aligned}$

